        "lines": [
          "The organelle that contains the chlorophyll",
          "pigments is the chloroplast.",
          "It is bounded by a double membrane — an outer",
          "membrane and an inner membrane — with a narrow",
          "space between them.",
          "The inner membrane encloses a ground substance",
          "called the stroma."
        ],
        "why": "Naming the organelle and its double envelope sets up everything else, because both the grana and the stroma lie inside that envelope.",
